**[goal]** Fix `HookBus` so it matches the README contract, without touching the public API, `./test`, or dependencies.

**[action]** Diagnosed `src/bus.ts` `emit`:

```ts
list.forEach(async (handler) => { await handler(payload); });
```

`forEach` ignores the promise each callback returns, so every handler started at once, `emit` resolved immediately, and a throw/reject became an unhandled rejection instead of rejecting `emit`. Replaced it with an ordered sequential loop over a snapshot:

```ts
const list = [...(this.handlers.get(event) ?? [])];
for (const handler of list) { await handler(payload); }
```

No signature changed; `on` and `count` untouched; `src/plugin.ts` needed no change (its one-time notice only skipped the *next* emit because of the bus bug making unsubscribes land mid-emit, and its async redaction only ran before the log line by luck of timing).

**[result]** All three symptoms trace to that one line:

- out of order / overlapping: `forEach` fanned out, so a slow async redaction finished after later handlers;
- hook never runs: `emit` returned before handlers settled, so work was dropped when the caller moved on (and any handler after an ignored throw still ran, masking errors);
- failing hook silently ignored: the rejected promise from an `async` `forEach` callback was never connected to `emit`'s promise.

**[next]** Proof, from `npm test` (10/10 pass, 0 fail): the 2 original tests unchanged plus 8 contract checks I added in `tmp/contract.test.ts` (outside `./test`) covering sequential order with a slow async handler, `emit` settling last, sync throw and async rejection both rejecting with the *same* error object and skipping later handlers, self-unsubscribe, unsubscribing another handler, subscribing during an emit, and the plugin (notice once, redaction, then audit line, in that order). Assumption: "one-time notice" means one notice per bus for all future emits, and concurrent `emit` calls are not part of the contract (each emit gets its own snapshot); the notice handler is idempotent enough that this cannot double-log within one emit sequence.
